Start (Green Oval)
Meaning: Indicates where the algorithm begins.
Action: Initialize the program and define the numbers list as .

"num" Assignment (Label/Text)
Meaning: num is defined as the first value in the numbers list.
Action: Sets up the first loop variable for processing.

Decision (Orange Diamond)
Meaning: A decision point checks if num is the last number in the sequence.
Action: Evaluates whether the current number is the last in the list.

Print Statement (Teal Parallelogram)
Meaning: Displays the value of num if it's not the last number.
Action: If the condition evaluates to "No," the program prints num.

Assignment Arrow (Horizontal Arrow)
Meaning: Moves to the next number in the list by reassigning num.
Action: Sets up next iteration with the following number in the list.

End (Red Oval)
Meaning: Signals where the process stops.
Action: Terminates the program when num is the last number in the list.

What The Flowchart Does
The flowchart starts with a predefined list of numbers: .
It assigns the first value to the variable num.
For each iteration, the program checks: Is num the last number? If No, it prints num and assigns the next number to num.
This loop continues until num is the last number in the list, at which point the algorithm ends without printing that last number


